From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE leaves CPU-decoded images while EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC is on (as the collectors do); _CPU=1 lets them go, _CPU=0 keeps them always

Follow-up to 0885 (review, 13 Nov). 0885 deleted CPU-decoded (AsynchronousDecode) images by default.
The play settings (v3.4 line 87) set EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC=120, and with it every collector leaves
those images: the field's ground texture and its two 1365x1365x90 arrays take seconds of CPU
decoding each, show black meanwhile, and take 321 MiB of heap while both decode (texture_cache.h,
KeepAsyncDecodedFrames' comment: the pressure collector made each of them new 5 to 7 times a walk).
A turn back into the field after a drop would bring that back.

Now: EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU exact "1": they go; exact "0": they stay; unset or anything else:
they stay while EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC is on, and go when it is off. Off (EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE
unset): unchanged, nothing runs. Same file as 0885 (texture_cache.h), not a translation id input,
no name in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index afe75bc78b5b4440ed4561d2ebbbb830fc73cb95..3b5ce31a5f98f79696e367aba392b5937a2c94f0 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -1327,8 +1327,9 @@ void TextureCache<P>::ShortPoolCollect() {
 // GPU did not write (no copy back, no staging, no GPU wait), not decoding. Unlike 0730 the costly
 // ones go too: an ASTC texture is decoded again on the GPU when it is used again; a CPU-decoded
 // one (the field's two 1365x1365x90 arrays: 4.5 s of decoding each in the logs of 13 Nov, and
-// 321 MiB of heap while both decode) is decoded on the CPU again, unless
-// EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU=0 keeps those. Where the front has no pool figure (FreeLargest 0) it
+// 321 MiB of heap while both decode, black meanwhile) is decoded on the CPU again only when
+// EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU=1; by default those stay while EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC is on (the
+// collectors' rule, in the play settings), and =0 keeps them always. Where the front has no pool figure (FreeLargest 0) it
 // does nothing; with the pool over <MiB> it deletes nothing.
 // Lines: stderr "EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE open ..." when a window opens and "... closed ..." when it
 // ends having deleted something; eden_log (HW.GPU) "EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE 600 frames: ..." with the
@@ -1379,13 +1380,19 @@ void TextureCache<P>::ShortPoolCollect() {
     return bytes;
 }
 
-/// EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU=0 (exact "0"): CPU-decoded images stay. Unset or anything else: they go.
+/// EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU: exact "1": CPU-decoded images go; exact "0": they stay; unset or
+/// anything else: they stay while EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC is on (as every collector leaves them:
+/// seconds of decoding each, black meanwhile, and 321 MiB of heap for the field's two arrays),
+/// and go when it is off.
 [[nodiscard]] inline bool AreaStaleDropsCpu() {
-    static const bool drops = [] {
+    static const int setting = [] {
         const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_CPU");
-        return !(value != nullptr && value[0] == '0' && value[1] == '\0');
+        if (value != nullptr && (value[0] == '0' || value[0] == '1') && value[1] == '\0') {
+            return value[0] - '0';
+        }
+        return -1;
     }();
-    return drops;
+    return setting == 1 || (setting < 0 && KeepAsyncDecodedFrames() == 0);
 }
 
 /// How many deleted addresses AreaStaleDrop remembers for its "made again" count.
